      "escalates_to": {
        "severity": "blocks",
        "when": "the product has end users outside the organisation",
        "requires": "a declaration by the owner under the threshold id end_users_outside_the_organisation (see adapters.thresholds), like any other threshold. True escalates the rule to blocks; false records the escalation as declined; no declaration is reported as an undeclared threshold, which is an escalation PENDING and not one declined. Written this way on 2026-10-29: the clause said through the same mechanism as any threshold and that mechanism is by threshold id, and no id existed for this one, so the absence of a key meant the two states at once and no auditor could tell them apart (D-076).",
