  "faces": {
    "what": "A face is a cut of the statement of one rule with an identifier of its own (CQ-19.1). Faces exist for a mechanical reason and not a drafting one: without an identifier a single one cannot be switched off, and a rule that can only be switched off whole pushes towards switching off too much. Their statement lives only in Annex H, like the statement of a rule, and the build extracts it (D-044).",
    "id_shape": "the id of the rule, a dot, and an ordinal that is never recycled: CQ-19.1",
    "ids_append_only": "A face is added; it is never renamed, never recycled and never changes meaning, exactly like a rule id.",
